[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human HeLa (ribonn)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=9,793): skew = 0.077, excess kurtosis = 0.179, D'Agostino K^2 p = 2.89e-05, Jarque-Bera p = 1.19e-05
  Normality of residuals: skew = -0.101, excess kurtosis = 0.505, D'Agostino K^2 p = 4.25e-19, Jarque-Bera p = 6.47e-27
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 217.180, p = 2.23e-19
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 78.792, p = 1.14e-34
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/ribonn/HeLa/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_te_histogram_ribonn_HeLa.png
